  "mathematical_proof_50pps": "Mathematical proof why 2.5s detection delay is unattainable for 50 pps single-source SYN flood: At 50 pps, transmitting 50 attack packets requires exactly Delta_t_packet = (50 - 1) / 50 = 0.980 s (980 ms). Because silent or dropped SYNs require the N = 2.000 s completion timeout to elapse before incomplete handshake status can be definitively established, the real end-to-end detection delay is Delta_t_real = Delta_t_packet + N_timeout = 0.980 s + 2.000 s = 2.980 s (~3.0 s). A delay <= 2.5 s is physically impossible unless the threshold is reduced below 25 pps (which would trigger false alarms on legitimate bursts) or timeout is reduced below 1.5 s (which would classify slow clients as attacks). Therefore, the Session 3 pre-registered criterion must be updated to <= 3.5 s for 50 pps low-rate attacks while maintaining <= 2.5 s for high-rate attacks.",
